// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6319 new: Rundll32 Execution of DLL Masquerading as Non-Executable File Type
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6319
// Pull request author: PpT2211
// Change: new rule
// Title: Rundll32 Export Call Against Document Or Data File Extension
// Sigma ID: 3e6b8f1a-2d5c-4a9e-b1f4-7c8d0a2e5f6b
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Pavan Pothamsetti (PpT2211)
// Date: 2026-08-28 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011, T1036.008
// Description: Detects rundll32.exe invoked with a document or data file extension (e.g. .txt, .pdf, .dat,
//   .tmp, .ini, .html, .js) immediately followed by a comma, i.e. in the "module,export" position.
//   rundll32 loads its first argument as a module regardless of extension, so adversaries rename a
//   malicious DLL to a benign-looking extension. This complements the existing image-extension and
//   uncommon-extension rules: it requires the export-call syntax, which keeps it narrower than the
//   uncommon-extension rule, and covers document/data extensions that the image-extension rule does
//   not. Execution with a msiexec.exe parent is excluded, since MSI custom actions routinely run
//   rundll32 against .tmp/.dat staging files.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate installers and updaters (e.g. Squirrel-based apps, some ClickOnce deployments) that stage payloads with non-standard extensions before invoking rundll32. Extend filter_main_msiexec if identified in your environment
//   - Rare help or media viewer integrations that pass non-DLL files to rundll32
// References:
//   - https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/infostealer-malware-formbook-spread-via-phishing-campaign-part-i
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/afa8c265b64cc6a4c53b6a09aae7a487029c90a0/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_doc_or_data_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".pdf," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".pdf\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".docx," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".docx\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ppt," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ppt\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".txt," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".txt\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".dat," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".dat\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".tmp," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".tmp\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ini," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ini\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".html," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".html\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".htm," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".htm\"," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".js," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".js\",")) and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\msiexec.exe"))
